I have updated the reference policy status page with a listing of the
remaining modules that need to be converted, and note which modules are
in the Fedora strict and targeted policies.

http://serefpolicy.sourceforge.net/index.php?page=status

For those looking to contribute, we ask that priority be given to the
modules in the targeted policy, and then strict policy.  I've attached
my notes on converting the old macros.  The big caveat is that not all
macros are expanded completely, for example the network macros, since
some are very complex because of the different expansions because of
different/optional parameters.  There is also no guarantee that there
are no errors, since its just my notes.  So to get from an old macro to
the end reference policy rules/interfaces, it may take a couple
expansions (especially in the network macros).

If you're looking to contribute, please let us know what you're working
on, so we can update the status page, and then work won't be duplicated.

